y is discarded once its status is adopted, so the first attempt stalls and the retry commits\\\"}],\n \\\"executions\\\":{},\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]}\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Recorded the client-completion result for the re-propose probe and promoted a Fact for the value-adoption line of work, with a new source range for the execution-time reply condition. The re-queue comparison holds, so the replacement decision does not silently consume the client request; the reply side is answered from source and registered as a partially resolved gap because the harness never ran the execution path.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-exec-reply\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"epaxos/exec.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":124,\\\"end_line\\\":142,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[fact],\n \\\"gaps\\\":[{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"602b7dcab8064d2ab9113ac315a40743-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does the replaced instance itself ever produce a client-visible reply, given that the owner's pending proposals are cleared when the replacement decision arrives?\\\"}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"602b7dcab8064d2ab9113ac315a40743-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"602b7dcab8064d2ab9113ac315a40743-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-commit-repropose\\\",\\\"s-exec-reply\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"f96da636a32f473280ce82dc0f0a002d\\\":[3,2,6,7,9,10,11,12]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"holds\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":None,\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: the protection around a replacement decision works as the source describes, and the client's request is not silently consumed. Measured in receipt f96da636a32f473280ce82dc0f0a002d (fixed experiment 602b7dcab8064d2ab9113ac315a40743-experiment, test TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoveryReproposesClientRequest, exit 0, 13 parsed events): the owner replica 0 proposed command X with a real GPropose (com